@startuml 4-5-line-closing
' 4-5. A message (text / image) arrives while the session is CLOSING - the sweeper is closing a silent session
' Traced from code at dev-rewrite e09d47b (2026-10-11) . box = file . arrow = function calls function
' italic = what that function does to PSQL / Redis
' CLOSING = session:{id}:state is CLOSING (set by session.start_closing in sweeper.sweep)
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
autonumber

title 4-5. Message arrives while the session is CLOSING

actor "LINE\n(reporter)" as LINE
participant "controllers/\nline.py" as CTRL
participant "workers/\nsweeper.py" as SWEEPER
participant "services/\nsession.py" as SESS
participant "services/\njob.py" as JOB
participant "clients/\ndatabase.py\n(PSQL)" as CDB
participant "clients/\nredis.py\n(Redis)" as CRD

== the sweeper starts closing a silent session ==
SWEEPER -> SWEEPER : sweep()
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.find_silent()
SESS -> CDB : select_silent_sessions(CLOSE_AFTER_MINUTES)\n<i>open sessions whose last_message_at is older than N minutes</i>
CDB --> SESS : [Session]
SESS --> SWEEPER : [Session]
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.start_closing(silent)
SESS -> CRD : set_closing_if_idle(session_id)\n<i>SET session:{id}:state CLOSING NX</i>
CRD --> SESS : True
SESS --> SWEEPER : True
note right of SWEEPER
  no key (IDLE) -> set succeeds -> state = CLOSING
  False (already BUFFERING, PROCESSING or CLOSING) -> skips this session
end note

== a new message hits the webhook now ==
LINE -> CTRL : POST /webhook/line -> ... -> on_message(event)
ref over CTRL, CRD
  same as 4-1 from user.find_by_line_id through session.buffer(message)
  session.open_for: the session is still open in PSQL -> same session, last_message_at = now()
  the message is saved to PSQL (pending) and appended to the buffer
end ref
CTRL -> SESS : session.start_buffering(current)
SESS -> CRD : set_buffering_if_idle(session_id)\n<i>SET session:{id}:state BUFFERING NX</i>
CRD --> SESS : False
SESS --> CTRL : False
note right of CTRL
  the key already exists (CLOSING) -> set fails
  job.enqueue_chat is not called
end note
CTRL --> LINE : 200 "OK"

== the sweeper continues - close fails, session is handed back ==
SWEEPER -> SWEEPER : finish_closing(silent)
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.close(silent)
SESS -> CDB : close_session(session_id, CLOSE_AFTER_MINUTES)\n<i>UPDATE sessions SET status = closed</i>\n<i>WHERE still open and still silent for more than N minutes</i>
CDB --> SESS : False
note right of SESS
  last_message_at just moved -> no row updated
  redis.clear_session is not called
end note
SESS --> SWEEPER : False
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.stop_closing(silent)
SESS -> CRD : clear_state(session_id)\n<i>DEL session:{id}:state -> IDLE</i>
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.has_buffer(silent)
SESS -> CRD : buffer_length(session_id)\n<i>LLEN session:{id}:buffer</i>
CRD --> SESS : 1
SESS --> SWEEPER : True
SWEEPER -> SESS : session.start_buffering(silent)
SESS -> CRD : set_buffering_if_idle(session_id)
CRD --> SESS : True
SESS --> SWEEPER : True
SWEEPER -> JOB : job.enqueue_chat(silent)
JOB -> CRD : push_job(Job(kind="chat", session_id))\n<i>RPUSH jobs</i>
note right of SWEEPER
  the worker takes this chat job and answers as in 4-2
  has_buffer returns False (nothing waiting) -> ends at IDLE, no job queued
end note

note over LINE, CRD
  a message that arrives after session.close has succeeded (session is closed in PSQL - 4-6)
  session.open_for opens a new session -> the new session has no state -> follows 4-1
end note
@enduml
